  "verbalization": "Pitavastatin and Alb are linked through a chain of molecular interactions involving Rosuvastatin, a known HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor. The evidence suggests that Pitavastatin causes Myoglobin Urine Present or Myoglobinuria, both of which are mediated by Rosuvastatin. Rosuvastatin, in turn, binds to Alb, implying a direct interaction between the two entities. The shared lowest common ancestor, Pitavastatin and Rosuvastatin, both belonging to the class of HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors, reinforces a common pharmacological pathway. This suggests that Pitavastatin may influence Alb through its interaction with Rosuvastatin, potentially modulating Alb's activity or binding. The integrated explanation highlights a mechanistic link between Pitavastatin and Alb via Rosuvastatin, emphasizing the role of HMG-CoA reductase inhibition in this relationship.",
